e given constant $k$."] [:db/add "e423b9ad-3262-58aa-a896-09efb5972d47" :question/worked-solution "Newton's law of cooling states that the rate at which the temperature $T(t)$ of a body changes is proportional to the difference between its temperature and its surroundings. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-{T}_{S}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${T}_{S}$ is the temperature of the surroundings, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, ${T}_{S}={70}^{∘}\\text{F},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-70).\n$$"] [:db/add "e423b9ad-3262-58aa-a896-09efb5972d47" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "e423b9ad-3262-58aa-a896-09efb5972d47" :question/answer-fields "e15f2f6b-753f-59e6-83f9-114506d09104"] [:db/ensure "e423b9ad-3262-58aa-a896-09efb5972d47" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186078583 :knowledge-point/questions "e423b9ad-3262-58aa-a896-09efb5972d47"] [:db/add "521072eb-dac5-5936-bb4c-e2735ce83f05" :answer/id #uuid "521072eb-dac5-5936-bb4c-e2735ce83f05"] [:db/add "521072eb-dac5-5936-bb4c-e2735ce83f05" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "521072eb-dac5-5936-bb4c-e2735ce83f05" :answer/value "{T}^{′}(t)=kT(T+21)"] [:db/ensure "521072eb-dac5-5936-bb4c-e2735ce83f05" :answer/validate] [:db/add "83c6b4a3-aa03-5430-ab7c-03939204a89d" :answer/id #uuid "83c6b4a3-aa03-5430-ab7c-03939204a89d"] [:db/add "83c6b4a3-aa03-5430-ab7c-03939204a89d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "83c6b4a3-aa03-5430-ab7c-03939204a89d" :answer/value "{T}^{′}(t)=-kT(T-21)"] [:db/ensure "83c6b4a3-aa03-5430-ab7c-03939204a89d" :answer/validate] [:db/add "27a256eb-8879-56ff-99df-300971473e6f" :answer/id #uuid "27a256eb-8879-56ff-99df-300971473e6f"] [:db/add "27a256eb-8879-56ff-99df-300971473e6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "27a256eb-8879-56ff-99df-300971473e6f" :answer/value "{T}^{′}(t)=kT(T-21)"] [:db/ensure "27a256eb-8879-56ff-99df-300971473e6f" :answer/validate] [:db/add "95e22611-c98